{"position":{"x":2863,"y":940}},"children":[],"state":{"text":"I'll execute the gap analysis now. Starting with data load and proceeding through all phases silently.Good. `gap_analysis.json` is empty (re-invocation guard passes). All required files loaded successfully. Proceeding with requirement extraction and analysis.\n\nThe candidate has:\n- Bachelor of Biomedical Science from La Trobe (completed 2023) — matches required qualification\n- Expired First Aid (2022)\n- Retail work history (Bunnings 2024–present, Coles 2020–2024) — no laboratory experience\n- Basic technical skills (Microsoft Word, POS)\n- No laboratory-specific technical skills, LIMS experience, or analyser experience\n\nNow building the full requirements array, matching against candidate profile, and constructing strengths/gaps.The validator tool timed out. Proceeding to read the verdict file directly.The validator has issued a REJECT verdict with 4 blocking issues. All four concern false-positive strengths — curriculum-inferred or assumption-based claims not explicitly documented in the CV.\n\nRe-reading the candidate profile to confirm:\n\nThe CV contains:\n- Education: Bachelor of Biomedical Science (La Trobe University, completed 2023)\n- Work history: Bunnings (Team Member, 2024-present), Coles (Checkout Operator, 2020-2024)\n- No explicit mention of: pipetting, specimen handling, laboratory safety, quality assurance/control, medical terminology, biochemistry test panels, or shift patterns (weekend/public holiday)\n\nThe validator is correct. The curriculum-implied exception was over-applied. These are substantive knowledge/skill claims that require explicit demonstration in the CV, not curriculum inference alone.\n\nApplying fixes: removing four strengths (strength_2, strength_3, strength_4, strength_5 → IDs strength_2, strength_3, strength_4, strength_5) and creating corresponding gaps.# ✓ Analyst Complete\n\n4 strengths, 10 gaps identified.\n\nTop strength: Bachelor of Science (Biomedical Science, Biochemistry, Medical Laboratory Science, or closely related discipline) from a recognised Australian or equivalent institution\n\nKey gap: Demonstrated understanding of basic laboratory practices, including pipetting techniques, specimen handling, and laboratory safety (severity: High)","dispatchOnSet":false,"size":{"width":324,"height":418}},"type":"text","groupId":"{#}Aemc6B1"},"{#}8EK4KL3":{"id":"{#}8EK4KL3","canvas":{"position":{"x":3044,"y":871}},"children":[],"state":{},"type":"output","groupId":"{#}Aemc6B1"},"{#}DE3sdXo":{"id":"{#}DE3sdXo","canvas":{"position":{"x":3045,"y":597}},"children":[],"state":{"name":"Agent Outputs.analyst_output","reactive":false,"lastConfiguration":{"controlType":"multilineText","controlSettings":{"value":"","placeholder":"Enter text..."},"group":"Agent Outputs"}},"type":"globalVariable","groupId":"{#}Aemc6B1"},"{#}KtY9l4c":{"id":"{#}KtY9l4c","canvas":{"position":{"x":3049,"y":676}},"children":[],"state":{"name":"Agent Reasoning.analyst_reasoning","reactive":false,"lastConfiguration":{"controlType":"multilineText","controlSettings":{"placeholder":"Enter text...","group":"agentReasoning"},"group":"Agent Reasoning"}},"type":"globalVariable","groupId":"{#}Aemc6B1"},"{#}fde08Db":{"id":"{#}fde08Db","canvas":{"position":{"x":3046,"y":768}},"children":[],"state":{"name":"Agent Debug.analyst_debug","reactive":false,"lastConfiguration":{"controlType":"anything","controlSettings":{"value":null},"group":"Agent Debug"}},"type":"globalVariable","groupId":"{#}Aemc6B1"},"{#}rH1ZfcX":{"id":"{#}rH1ZfcX","canvas":{"position":{"x":2839,"y":82}},"children":[{"childId":"{#}ymhMAzR","sourcePort":"{#}rH1ZfcX_innerOutput_inner-input-input-pL33Gf","targetPort":"{#}ymhMAzR_input_input"}],"state":{"description":"","inputs":[{"name":"input-pL33Gf","description":"Tool input data","type":[6],"label":"input","index":0,"position":{"x":757,"y":433}}],"outputs":[],"name":"ChangeAgent","type":"custom","color":"#4e3eff","canvasPosition":{"x":702.352978730763