1.1992-808.8z\"/>\n <path d=\"m739.2 1028.4-22.801 7.1992c-32.398 8.3984-51.602 42-43.199 75.602 7.1992 27.602 32.398 45.602 58.801 45.602 4.8008 0 10.801-1.1992 15.602-2.3984 9.6016-2.3984 19.199-6 28.801-8.3984 32.398-10.801 49.199-45.602 38.398-76.801-8.4023-33.602-43.199-51.602-75.602-40.805z\"/>\n <path d=\"m532.8 1046.4-24-3.6016c-33.602-7.1992-66 14.398-72 48-7.1992 33.602 14.398 66 48 72 9.6016 2.3984 20.398 3.6016 30 4.8008 2.3984 0 6 1.1992 9.6016 1.1992 30 0 56.398-21.602 60-52.801 4.7969-33.598-18.004-64.797-51.602-69.598z\"/>\n <path d=\"m321.6 955.2c-26.398-20.398-64.801-16.801-86.398 9.6016-20.398 26.398-16.801 64.801 9.6016 86.398 8.3984 6 15.602 12 24 18 10.801 7.1992 22.801 10.801 34.801 10.801 19.199 0 38.398-8.3984 50.398-26.398 19.199-27.602 13.199-66-14.398-85.199z\"/>\n <path d=\"m192 793.2c-14.398-31.199-50.398-44.398-81.602-30-31.199 14.398-44.398 50.398-30 81.602 4.8008 9.6016 8.3984 18 13.199 27.602 10.801 20.398 32.398 32.398 54 32.398 9.6016 0 19.199-2.3984 28.801-7.1992 30-15.602 40.801-52.801 25.199-82.801z\"/>\n <path d=\"m800.4 657.6-140.4-90v-223.2c0-33.602-27.602-61.199-61.199-61.199-33.602 0-61.199 27.602-61.199 61.199v256.8c0 20.398 10.801 40.801 28.801 51.602l168 106.8c9.6016 6 21.602 9.6016 32.398 9.6016 20.398 0 39.602-9.6016 51.602-28.801 17.996-27.602 9.5977-64.801-18.004-82.801z\"/>\n</svg>\n","inputs":[{"name":"agent","description":"Connect to the agent","type":5}],"outputs":[{"name":"getHistory","description":"Invoked when the agent needs to retrieve the conversation history","type":5},{"name":"updateHistory","description":"Invoked when the agent needs to update the conversation history","type":5}],"color":"#eac43e"}],"publicationId":"kemu.io.ai-agent-osx-arm64-1.9.1","sessionId":1784443105}},"type":"hubService","secrets":{"OPENROUTER_API_KEY":{"name":"OPENROUTER_API_KEY","sharedAcrossInstances":true,"hubServiceName":"kemu.io.ai-agent"}},"groupId":"{#}EnyQUlO"},"{#}63UMJIM":{"id":"{#}63UMJIM","canvas":{"position":{"x":2263.3619384765625,"y":1371.4234008789062}},"children":[],"state":{"text":"done — verdict written to analyst_validator_verdict.json","dispatchOnSet":false,"size":{"width":452,"height":506}},"type":"text","groupId":"{#}EnyQUlO"},"{#}H2HWNwV":{"id":"{#}H2HWNwV","canvas":{"position":{"x":2231.3619384765625,"y":2094.4234008789062}},"children":[],"state":{"text":"**Reviewing Gap Analysis**\n\nI'm currently processing the `gap_analysis.json` file as instructed. My focus is on absorbing its contents to understand the identified discrepancies. This forms the foundation for further evaluation.\n\n**Auditing Found Files**\n\nI've successfully loaded `gap_analysis.json`, `candidate_profile.json`, and `enhanced_jd.json`. My next step is to meticulously review the `gap_analysis.json` for any semantic discrepancies, ensuring all true gaps are identified and false positives are excluded, by comparing it against the candidate and job description data.\n\n**Analyzing Candidate Skills**\n\nI'm currently scrutinizing the `gap_analysis.json`, specifically focusing on how the candidate's Bachelor of Biomedical Science fulfills \"Basic laboratory practices.\" While a curriculum is implied, I'm questioning whether it objectively proves the required practical skills without explicit project evidence, as per the \"emphasize any laboratory practicals\" guideline.\n\n**Evaluating Skill Assertions**\n\nI'm questioning the validity of certain strengths identified, particularly those attributed solely to the candidate's curriculum without explicit CV evidence of practical application. I'm flagging \"Basic laboratory practices,\" \"Understanding of medical terminology,\" and \"Basic knowledge of QA/QC\" as potential gaps due to a lack of direct support on the CV.\n\n**Refining Skill Assessment**\n\nI'm re-evaluating the retail experience, specifically questioning the classification of \"retail shift work\" as a \"direct\" skill. It appears this was inferred, not explicitly stated in the CV, and I'm now flagging roster/shift availability as a potential gap due to this lack of explicit evidence, rather than a domain skill.\n\n**Verifying Candidate Skills**\n\nI'm confirming that \"Transferable via Customer Service\" for `req_5` and \"Transferable via Team player\" for `req_6` are indeed valid, as they align with the candidate's profile. My current focus is on identifying the specific instances of hallucinated strengths within the `gap_analysis.json`, particularly around laboratory practices and QA/QC, as the CV lacks direct evidence for these.\n\n**Identifying Skill Gaps**\n\nI'm revisiting the curriculum-based strengths, specifically the assumptions made about \"Basic laboratory practices\" and \"Understanding of medical terminology.\" The CV's silence on explicit demonstration necessitates these be marked as gaps, especially considering the ATS recommendation for specific keyword inclusion.\n\n**Confirming Hallucinated Strengths**\n\nI've identified four clear instances where strengths were assumed from the candidate's curriculum rather than being directly evidenced on their CV. These include specific laboratory practices, QA/QC knowledge, retail shift experience, and medical terminology. Each of these will be reclassified as gaps.\n\n**Re-evaluating Requirement 2**\n\nI'm questioning if \"Basic laboratory practices\" (strengths[1]) is truly a gap. While the CV lacks explicit mention of pipetting or specimen handling, the recommendation guides emphasize foundational knowledge from coursework. I'm also noting that gap_7 is missing, despite requirements 2, 3, 8, and pref_6 being marked as strengths.\n\n","dispatchOnSet":false,"size":{"width":487,"height":630}},"type":"text","groupId":"{#}EnyQUlO"},"{#}tCj7Q60":{"id":"{#}tCj7Q60","canvas":{"position":{"x":2395.3619384765625,"y":1097.4234008789062}},"children":[{"childId":"{#}WO4nCzE","sourcePort":"{#}tCj7Q60_innerOutput_inner-input-input-pL33Gf","targetPort":"{#}WO4nCzE_input_input"}],"state":{"description":"","i